message.content:
I found two possible lesions. Neither is a clear call, and you should treat this as a screening result, not a diagnosis.

```json
{"lesions": [
  {"box": [0.279, 0.615, 0.319, 0.687], "pai": 3},
  {"box": [0.594, 0.284, 0.623, 0.347], "pai": 3}
]}
```

1. **Lower right, under the bridge (image left).** The root tip of the root-filled back tooth has a patch of thinner, darker bone around it. It looks like some mineral loss, but it has no clear radiolucent border, so I graded it PAI 3.
2. **Upper left (image right), between the roots of the root-filled teeth under the crown.** There is a darker area here. It may be the maxillary sinus dipping down between the roots rather than a lesion: it has a curved, cortex-like lower border, which a sinus would have. This one is the less certain of the two; I graded it PAI 3.

I didn't see a well-defined periapical radiolucency anywhere, so neither finding reaches PAI 4 or 5. To check these, I zoomed into the regions and boosted the contrast. Panoramic images blur and overlap structures, so a periapical X-ray of these two areas would be needed to confirm or rule them out.
